  "scope": "Finite original-pixel stationary filing at an independently owned upward-cutting vise bench. Visible near-boot support, actual metal/cutting-arc proximity0-4, lift/return5-7 and task lifecycle reviewed. Hidden previously occluded body/far sole, forces, material removal, economy, tool pickup/put-down, directions and repeat excluded.",
  "checks": {
    "identity-and-scale": "Original bald stocky Blacksmith, split dark brass-bound beard, cream sleeves and leather apron. All selected opaque original0-7 body/near-boot/hands/file pixels exact. One actual opaque533/[320,616] pose0 basis and maximum4px integer whole-pose registration. No local painting, body warp, per-pose scaling, mirror, duplicate pose or synthetic in-between. Formerly occluded far leg/body remains unobserved and unreconstructed.",
    "station-and-foot-contact": "Visible stationary near-boot material minimum correlation0.982451, maximum travel3.688213px and adjacent3.140063px pass unchanged.94/6/6 limits. Independent furniture uses the same533/[320,616] physical root basis. One fixed whole-prop placement only; native/game occlusion inspected. No hidden sole, traveling gait, ground force or cross-direction height approval.",
    "hand-and-tool-contact": "The same file stays held between the two hands through forward stroke0-4 and lift/return5-7. Actually visible metal shaft-edge points lie within5.881286px of the true opaque upward cutting arc, below6px, during0-4. First shadow/handle-adjacent0 proposal discarded for directly inspected gray lower shaft edge. Recovery distances remain recorded without a pressure claim. No hidden underside, 3D force or burr/material removal certified.",
    "prop-continuity": "Actor owns original body, hands, file and visible near boot. Independent bench owns the four-legged table, shelf tools/fasteners, fixed screw vise and single deeply clamped upward-cutting blade. Three ordered builtin prop edits retained; first two fixtures unselected. Only uniform normalization and fixed whole-prop placement used. All8 layers and actual game captures show one fixed vise/blade, without a carried-file fragment in furniture or spontaneous in-cycle transfer. Bench/blade persists after departure; no completed sharpening or resource reward.",
    "completion-and-reset": "Seven actual forge days show every authored-duration filing frame, one completion at7 and an unchanged5-second finish. Camera rotation preserves held task state. Cancel releases actor; independent vise/bench/blade persists after departure. Explicit return resets0, day resolution releases motion and day7 restores first forging operation. This is one finite filing stroke/recovery, not a seamless repeat or certified pickup/put-down transition."
  },
